u cell  analyzer for accountant viability  measurements  results for the muse immunology assays  are shown here  the muse immunology assays provide  absolute counts total lymphocyte counts  and population percentages  based on the total lymphocyte population  for either cd4 cd8 or b cells  two of the assays are highlighted here  the dot plots in the upper left  highlight the results for either the cd4  assay or the cd8 assay  the lymphocyte population is shown on  the y-axis for both plots and either the  cd4 or the cd8 population is shown in  the x-axis  very clear separation for the lymphocyte  populations is shown for both assays as  well as clear separation for the cd4 as  well as the cd8 population  a comparison of the cd4 counts for a  predicate method versus the mu cell  analyzer is shown in the graph on the  right  you can see that based on the linear  response that is shown  based on both the slope as well as the r  squared value that comparable results  are seen on both on the mu cell analyzer  lastly we evaluated the cv  results for the count the percent  lymphocyte as well as the count for the  total population  these results were compared for three  operators across three instruments  running four samples in triplicate  you can see that the cvs for all of  these populations were well below five  percent highlighting that not only the  precision within the assay but across  users and instruments is extremely  high  we took immune cell identification and  enumeration one step further on the  easytype platforms which have the  ability to evaluate up to 12 fluorescent  channels at one time  to do this we did a tab and nk analysis  using a blood control from an external  vendor  the dot plots show the gating strategy  and separation of the populations for  either the cd  check plus  sample or the cd check low sample  you can see that cd45 positive cells  were gated into a cd3 plot where we  looked at cd3 negative and cd3 positive  cells  our cd3 positive cells were then gated  into a cd4 versus cd8 plot  and our cd3 negative population was  gated into  a plot where we looked at cd19 b cells  and cd16 and 56 positive and k cells  you can see that the separation for all  of the populations are very clear very  clearly separated  for both the pod the plus as well as the  cd check glow  sample the graphs on the right  show the count  for  the various populations when compared to  the vendor specified values  the vendor lower limit is shown in red  the high limit is shown in pink and the  average value is shown in orange  the easy site results are shown in blue  as these results show for both the cd  check plus  low as well as regular samples  the vendor limits are the accounts are  well within the vendor limits  using fresh whole blood donors we then  decided to not only do a  tb and nk analysis on our samples but  also to evaluate the naive and memory  populations  shown here is an example from one such  donor  the data shows a similar gaining  strategy  as we saw on a previous slide getting  our cd45 positive cells into a three  pos into a cd3 gate where we looked at  the positive and the negative samples  and then taking our cd4 positive  cells and our cd8 positive cells in  doing a naive and memory analysis on  those  you can see that there's clear  identification of multiple important  immune cell populations from this simple  analysis utilizing only 10 microliters  of blood  one final area i would like to show  today is related to mechanism of action  studies during drug discovery  development and deployment  here we show an example of the  mitodamage assay that combines three  cellular health markers  to assess changes in mitochondrial  membrane potential apoptosis or cellular  death  this example deploys all three cell  health markers simultaneously  medicine spread detects changes in  mitochondrial membrane potential and is  shown as a downward shift in  fluorescence  indicating a loss of the membrane  potential  apoptosis is detected using an exon 5  which indicates phosphatidylserine  exposure  lastly cellular death is detected using  7ad  staining  where there's a loss of membrane  integrity integrity  the dot plots shown here show example  stainings for the assay on jerk cats  clear separation for each population is  seen  the two bar graphs show dose responses  for either a topicide  a known  topoka isomerase inhibitor or  styrosporin a known protein kinase  inhibitor  and the corresponding population  percentages  with depolarized populations shown in  red  apoptotic populations shown in yellow  yellow  and cellular death population shown in  blue the bar graph is shown for both  compound depolarization and apoptosis  see similar percentages but little  cellular death was seen additionally at  this time point sterosphorin shows a  much larger shift  in depolarization and apoptosis when  compared to atopicide therefore in  addition to counting an immune cell  subpopulation identification  the guava platforms can be used to  evaluate and assess drug mechanism of  actions and effects  thank you  now i'll turn it over to stephanie  next we'll talk about the amnes cell  stream which is based off of the same  tdi ccd technology as the image stream  and flow site which brian talked about  earlier  the cell stream system is a benchtop  camera based flow cytometer built on the  amis technology similar to the image  stream an image gallery is used to  visualize objects in flow the cell  stream is a high throughput compact  system with a small footprint and it  allows for modular and flexible upgrades  the high sensitivity of the slow  cytometer allows for traditional flow  assays as well as small particle  experimentation  the cell stream can be used for  traditional assays such as  immunophenotyping  in this particular study we performed a  16 color amino phenotyping of major  lymphocytes and myeloid subsets in human  pvmcs and whole blood  as you can see we easily resolve all 